<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.4.1: Exponent Rules</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01297</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.4.1: Exponent Rules</md:title>
    <md:uuid>55a3b4f0-bbbb-4f23-a164-d2e34e894ecf</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <para>Find the value of \(x\) that makes the equation true.</para>
</list>
<para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise id="bce4fcf6-8203-4fce-826f-388d9a3e712a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(2^3\cdot 2^4=2^x\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is 7.</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 7</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d8c2ac02-4b93-4a46-8952-d7fceb46ebfd" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(2^5\cdot 2=2^x\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is 6.</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 6</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="abf28cef-62e8-4025-b358-1e0f5aacfbdd" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(2^{10}\div 2^7=2^x\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is 3.</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 3</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_63ed77a7-3fbe-4b8f-8127-de0820813702" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>\(2^9\div 2=2^x\)</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The answer is 8.</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: 8</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
